    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31NVjoFCMQL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: "/nordictrack-commercial-2450-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "About $2,299 (Amazon, 6 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":2299,"high":2299},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. belt · 4.25 CHP (NordicTrack rating) · 0–14 mph · -3% to 12% incline · 400 lb max user · folds",
    pros: [
      "The same iFIT classes as the t22.9, from Freemotion’s sister brand",
      "A 400 lb maximum user weight and a 22-inch belt, by NordicTrack’s figures",
      "A 14 mph top speed and a decline to -3% as well as a 12% incline",
      "A 24-inch touchscreen, for about a fifth of the t22.9’s price",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A consumer build and warranty, not Freemotion’s commercial construction",
      "The touchscreen is designed around an iFIT Pro membership at $39 a month",
      "NordicTrack’s motor warranty terms vary by listing; check them before ordering",
